The '''2026 FA Cup final''' was a [[Association football|football]] match played at [[Wembley Stadium]] in [[London]], England, on 16 May 2026 between [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] and [[Manchester City F.C.|Manchester City]] to determine the winners of the [[2025–26 FA Cup]]. It was the [[List of FA Cup finals|145th final]] of English football's primary cup competition, the [[FA Cup|Football Association Challenge Cup]].

Chelsea played in their 17th FA Cup final and the first since [[2022 FA Cup final|2022]], when they lost for a record third consecutive time.<ref name="semi-final1-report">{{Cite web |date=26 April 2026|title=Chelsea reach FA Cup final with 1-0 win over Leeds United |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/sport/football/chelsea-reach-fa-cup-final-with-1-0-win-over-leeds?ref=top-stories |agency=[[Reuters]] |access-date=26 April 2026|website=[[The Straits Times]] }}</ref> They were seeking a ninth Cup title. Manchester City played in their 15th FA Cup final overall and the fourth consecutively, the first ever team to do so.<ref name="semi-final2-report">{{Cite web |date=25 April 2026|title=Man City fight back to beat Southampton and reach fourth straight FA Cup final |url=https://www.straitstimes.com/sport/football/man-city-fight-back-to-beat-southampton-and-reach-fourth-straight-fa-cup-final |agency=Reuters|access-date=25 April 2026|website=[[The Straits Times]] }}</ref> They were seeking an eighth Cup title.

The clubs' most recent meeting in a title-deciding match was the [[2021 UEFA Champions League final]], which Chelsea won 1–0. The two sides have never before met in an FA Cup final, but have clashed in other domestic title-deciding matches, most recently in the [[2019 EFL Cup final]] and the [[2018 FA Community Shield]], both of which City won. They met twice in the [[2025–26 Premier League|season's Premier League]], a 1–1 draw in Manchester followed by City's 3–0 win in London.

Manchester City won 1–0 in the match, through a goal from [[Antoine Semenyo]], achieving their 8th FA Cup title.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/story/_/id/48785885/chelsea-man-city-live-latest-updates-fa-cup-final-commentary-score-result |title=Chelsea vs Man City: Antoine Semenyo scores the winner as Man City lift FA Cup - as it happened |publisher=ESPN |date=16 May 2026 }}</ref>

